# An allowlist: everything is out of the build context, and only what the image
# is built from comes back in. A deny list would let the next environment file,
# key, or state directory into the context by simply being new.
*
!.python-version
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!src
!frontend

# What the build makes for itself, so this machine's copy never travels.
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store
**/__pycache__
**/dist
**/.slidev

# The two trees above are admitted whole, so what must never be in an image is
# named again here: a secret or a key nested inside one of them would otherwise
# ride in on its parent directory.
**/.env*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_*
**/.npmrc
**/.git
